[
  {
    "id": "s1",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "In the year 2000, this was the most admired company in America.",
    "pose": "present",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "ENRON"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s2",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "Fortune magazine named it the most innovative company in America — six years in a row.",
    "text": "6 years running",
    "sub": "\"America's Most Innovative Company\"",
    "icon": "trophy"
  },
  {
    "id": "s3",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "At the top sat the founder, Ken Lay — a preacher's son turned energy tycoon, with friends in the highest offices in Washington.",
    "pose": "present",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "capitol",
        "label": "Ken Lay"
      },
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "…the founder"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s4",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "His protégé, Jeff Skilling, was the true believer — the man who'd turn a boring energy firm into a financial magic act.",
    "pose": "present",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "Jeff Skilling"
      },
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "…the believer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s5",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Enron. An energy company from Houston that seemed to turn everything it touched into gold.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "oilbarrel",
        "label": "energy"
      },
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "…into gold"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s6",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "Its stock hit ninety dollars. The company was worth seventy billion. The seventh biggest in the country.",
    "text": "$70 billion",
    "sub": "Enron at its peak",
    "icon": "chartup"
  },
  {
    "id": "s7",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Wall Street loved it. Harvard taught it. Everyone wanted a piece.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "bank",
        "label": "Wall Street"
      },
      {
        "name": "crowd",
        "label": "everyone wanted in"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s8",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "And then, in under a month, all of it simply… vanished.",
    "pose": "surprised",
    "expression": "surprised",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "ENRON"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…gone"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s9",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "Enron filed the largest bankruptcy in American history. Twenty thousand people lost their jobs — and their savings.",
    "text": "20,000 jobs",
    "sub": "gone, almost overnight",
    "icon": "crowd"
  },
  {
    "id": "s10",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "So where did seventy billion dollars actually go?",
    "pose": "think",
    "bubble": "Where did $70B go?",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "$70 billion"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…vanished?"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s11",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Here's the twist that still messes with people. The money didn't go anywhere. It was never really there.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "the money…"
      },
      {
        "name": "bubble",
        "label": "…was never real"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s12",
    "type": "title",
    "narration": "Let's follow money that never existed — all the way down.",
    "heading": "How Enron Made Its Money Disappear",
    "kicker": "The $70 billion magic trick",
    "sub": "It's not where the money went. It's that it was never there."
  },
  {
    "id": "s13",
    "type": "screenshot",
    "narration": "And this isn't me being dramatic — the admiration is right there in the public record.",
    "sourceId": "wiki-enron"
  },
  {
    "id": "s14",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Enron threw the best parties, hired the top graduates, and bragged it had reinvented business itself.",
    "pose": "present",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "trophy",
        "label": "the best & brightest"
      },
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "…'reinvented business'"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s15",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "The more untouchable a company feels, the fewer questions anyone dares to ask. That's lesson one.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "untouchable"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…so nobody asks"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s16",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "And it all rested on one magic number — the stock price. Keep it up, and the illusion holds.",
    "text": "Keep the stock up.",
    "sub": "…or the whole thing falls",
    "icon": "chartup"
  },
  {
    "id": "s17",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Enron didn't just sell oil and gas. It claimed it could trade anything — electricity, weather, even internet bandwidth.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "oilbarrel",
        "label": "energy"
      },
      {
        "name": "ticker",
        "label": "…trade anything"
      },
      {
        "name": "globe",
        "label": "even bandwidth"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s18",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "It called itself the company that would run the world's energy. And for a while, the whole world believed it.",
    "pose": "present",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "globe",
        "label": "run the world's energy"
      },
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "…and we believed"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s19",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Inside, Jeff Skilling ran it like a pressure cooker. Every year, the bottom ten percent of staff were simply fired.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "crowd",
        "label": "rank the staff"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…bottom 10% fired"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s20",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "They called it rank and yank. It bred brilliant people and ruthless sharks in equal measure.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "scale",
        "label": "rank & yank"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…geniuses & sharks"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s21",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "And behind the genius image, Enron was quietly gaming an entire state.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "globe",
        "label": "a whole state"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…being gamed"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s22",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "In 2000 and 2001, its traders helped trigger blackouts across California — then bet on the chaos they caused.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "California blackouts"
      },
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "…bet on the chaos"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s23",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "On recorded calls, traders joked about taking money from 'Grandma Millie.' That was the culture under the trophies.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "ticker",
        "label": "'Grandma Millie'"
      },
      {
        "name": "trophy",
        "label": "…under the awards"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s24",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "But the stock kept climbing. So nobody looked too hard.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "chartup",
        "label": "stock climbs"
      },
      {
        "name": "crowd",
        "label": "…nobody looks"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s25",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "To pull this off, Enron needed two magic tricks. Here's the first.",
    "pose": "present",
    "bubble": "Trick #1",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "trick one"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s26",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Normally, a company earns money, then writes it down. Simple.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "earn it"
      },
      {
        "name": "paystub",
        "label": "…then book it"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s27",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Enron's CEO, Jeff Skilling, had a better idea. Why wait for the money?",
    "pose": "present",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "why wait?"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s28",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "It's called mark-to-market accounting. Sign a twenty-year deal today…",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "iou",
        "label": "a 20-year deal"
      },
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "mark-to-market"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s29",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "…and book all twenty years of imagined profit, right now, as if it already happened.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "conjure the profit"
      },
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "…today"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s30",
    "type": "screenshot",
    "narration": "This is a real, legitimate method — for things that actually have a market price. Enron used it on deals that didn't.",
    "sourceId": "wiki-mtm"
  },
  {
    "id": "s31",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Guess at a future profit. Declare it real. Count it today. The cash? That part was optional.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "guess a profit"
      },
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "cash: optional"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s32",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "So on paper, Enron grew every single quarter. On paper.",
    "text": "On paper.",
    "sub": "the profits were projections, not cash",
    "icon": "newspaper"
  },
  {
    "id": "s33",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "If the real profit never showed up? Didn't matter. It was already counted.",
    "pose": "shrug",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "chartup",
        "label": "booked already"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…never arrived"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s34",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Wall Street saw the growth and cheered. The stock climbed. And the trap was set.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "bank",
        "label": "Wall St. cheers"
      },
      {
        "name": "chartup",
        "label": "stock climbs"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s35",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "To see how insane this gets, take one real deal. Enron teamed up with Blockbuster to stream movies to your home.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "newspaper",
        "label": "the Blockbuster deal"
      },
      {
        "name": "officetower",
        "label": "…stream movies"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s36",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "This was years before streaming even worked. The service barely launched.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "streaming? not yet"
      },
      {
        "name": "chartdown",
        "label": "…it flopped"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s37",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "Enron still booked over a hundred million dollars of profit from it. The project delivered almost nothing.",
    "text": "$110 million",
    "sub": "\"profit\" from a deal that flopped",
    "icon": "magichat"
  },
  {
    "id": "s38",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "The movies never streamed. The profit was already counted. That is mark-to-market in one story.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "profit booked"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…product never came"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s39",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "And regulators had actually blessed the method back in 1992. A legitimate tool…",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "capitol",
        "label": "SEC blessed it, '92"
      },
      {
        "name": "scale",
        "label": "a real tool…"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s40",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "…handed to people who decided that imagination counted as income.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "…imagination"
      },
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "= income"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s41",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Every quarter, Skilling needed a bigger number. So every quarter, the imagined profits grew.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "chartup",
        "label": "bigger each quarter"
      },
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "…invent more"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s42",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "It was a treadmill, speeding up, with no off switch.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "refinance",
        "label": "a treadmill"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…no off switch"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s43",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "And there was no room to miss. Wall Street expected Enron to beat its targets every single quarter, forever.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "bank",
        "label": "beat EVERY quarter"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…forever"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s44",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Miss once, and the stock drops, the shells wobble, the trick is exposed. So they never missed. They simply couldn't afford to.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "chartdown",
        "label": "miss = exposed"
      },
      {
        "name": "magichat",
        "label": "…so they faked it"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s45",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "But fake profits plus real spending equals a very real problem. Debt. Mountains of it.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "fake profit"
      },
      {
        "name": "iou",
        "label": "+ real debt"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…a problem"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s46",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "And debt scares investors. If the debt shows, the magic stops. So Enron had to hide it.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "iou",
        "label": "the debt"
      },
      {
        "name": "crowd",
        "label": "investors panic"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…hide it"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s47",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Enter the second magician. The CFO, Andrew Fastow.",
    "pose": "present",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "the CFO, Fastow"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s48",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "His solution? Invent companies. Fake ones. Hundreds, then thousands of them.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "shell companies"
      },
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "…thousands"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s49",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "Enron built around three thousand of these shell entities. With names like LJM, Chewco, and Raptor.",
    "text": "~3,000 shells",
    "sub": "LJM · Chewco · Raptor",
    "icon": "shellbox"
  },
  {
    "id": "s50",
    "type": "screenshot",
    "narration": "They're called special-purpose entities — real tools, bent into a hiding place.",
    "sourceId": "wiki-spe"
  },
  {
    "id": "s51",
    "type": "doodle",
    "narration": "Here's the move. Enron shoves its debt and its worst assets into a shell company…",
    "items": [
      "crookedE",
      "shellbox",
      "iou"
    ],
    "labels": [
      "ENRON",
      "→ a shell",
      "→ debt hidden"
    ],
    "flow": true
  },
  {
    "id": "s52",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "…and poof — the debt is off Enron's books. The company looks clean. Healthy. Unstoppable.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "debt vanishes"
      },
      {
        "name": "crookedE",
        "label": "…Enron looks clean"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s53",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "It's like opening a credit card in a fake friend's name, buying everything, then telling the bank you owe nothing.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "creditcard",
        "label": "fake friend's card"
      },
      {
        "name": "bank",
        "label": "…'I owe zero'"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s54",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Technically true. Completely insane. And for a while, completely legal-looking.",
    "pose": "shrug",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "scale",
        "label": "'technically true'"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…insane"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s55",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "And Fastow didn't only build the shells to help Enron. He built them to help himself.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "the shells"
      },
      {
        "name": "coins",
        "label": "…help himself"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s56",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "He personally ran some of the funds that were doing deals with Enron. He sat on both sides of the table.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "variant": "villain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "scale",
        "label": "both sides"
      },
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "…he ran LJM"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s57",
    "type": "callout",
    "narration": "Fastow secretly pocketed around forty-five million dollars for himself off these deals.",
    "text": "$45 million",
    "sub": "Fastow's personal cut",
    "icon": "coins"
  },
  {
    "id": "s58",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "And the board knew. They voted to waive their own ethics rules — twice — to let him do it.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "capitol",
        "label": "the board knew"
      },
      {
        "name": "scale",
        "label": "…waived ethics, twice"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s59",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "The shells got cartoon-villain names. Chewco, after Chewbacca. Raptor, after Jurassic Park. An inside joke.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "Chewco · Raptor"
      },
      {
        "name": "bubble",
        "label": "…an inside joke"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s60",
    "type": "doodle",
    "narration": "The pattern, three thousand times: a bad asset goes in, the debt disappears, and Enron keeps smiling.",
    "items": [
      "iou",
      "shellbox",
      "crookedE"
    ],
    "labels": [
      "bad asset in",
      "→ debt hidden",
      "→ Enron 'clean'"
    ],
    "flow": true
  },
  {
    "id": "s61",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "A labyrinth of three thousand shells, built specifically so nobody could ever follow the money.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "×3,000"
      },
      {
        "name": "warning",
        "label": "…a labyrinth"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s62",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Think of each shell as a closet. Enron stuffed its debt and its failures inside, and shut the doors.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
        "label": "a closet"
      },
      {
        "name": "iou",
        "label": "…shove the debt in"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s63",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "Then it photographed only the tidy rooms, and showed Wall Street the pictures.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "newspaper",
        "label": "show the tidy rooms"
      },
      {
        "name": "bank",
        "label": "…Wall Street applauds"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "s64",
    "type": "character",
    "narration": "But every closet was real debt that still had to be paid. Someone, someday, would open a door.",
    "pose": "explain",
    "props": [
      {
        "name": "shellbox",
